  "structure": {
    "block_count": 49,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Potty Training Resistance: Why Your Toddler Won’t Use the Potty — and How You Can Help",
        "text_sha256": "450d609f085ed026b5dda5b778a036f2c396809ab032bdd6ece4c20f7c628e42",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "resisting potty training, little toddler girl on the potty with her mom reading her a story",
        "text_sha256": "32f740f3e5955a732f248f13b946aa559875c735f11191914f7d9bb2b7dc138e",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Is your little one pushing back on potty training? Here are ways to make this stage go more smoothly for all of you.",
        "text_sha256": "a71e4e0d5ee50905d87f8dacc9bb653fdc7fbc65717c9487fb90c5b1c27617db",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There are plenty of signs indicating that your toddler is ready to be potty trained : He's at the right age, he's staying dry for longer stretches, and he follows you along to the bathroom to investigate what you're doing in there.",
        "text_sha256": "a3f71eaa887331e1bb51e8b226b3cbe6bab6fcfa615de2ea9570a87a13a848a3",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There's just one key sign that's missing: an actual desire to use the potty himself. Even though plenty of his peers are taking steps towards potty training, your tot is 100% uninterested in ditching his diapers.",
        "text_sha256": "3859a996ff34be916ceb997e64371da7ddf2f0d1845f1fd024cdb28d72ef1764",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Potty training resistance can be frustrating, not to mention challenging to navigate. (Should you try to just make him use the toilet? Or is that wrong?)",
        "text_sha256": "60e7d05e91a6ef2bd1119f41909e8a782545424cc2fbae9b9bd1aa62c3601e3c",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here are a few reasons your child might be putting on the bathroom brakes — and what you can do about it.",
        "text_sha256": "e5352c541af735b7e08622128802b0489a2a16cf306c46f9bb4c7daf1559ec70",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Potty resistance is normal. Many toddlers are physically ready but simply not interested yet — often because saying “no” is one of the few ways they can call the shots.",
        "text_sha256": "c248835342df57e8e18c395e7e5cd57da9b060c306756e5138da3fec241b6493",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Gentle patience beats pressure. The more you push, the more likely your little one is to push back. Giving choices, easing fears, and staying calm can help your child feel ready on his own terms.",
        "text_sha256": "26a88eb91d367c43e94ac1b8dde7777a25a435aa320afd0f3a3596033adc13a7",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Every child gets there at his own pace. Potty training isn’t a race — kids master this developmental skill on their own timeline.",
        "text_sha256": "eef45b53034fb1496bb3b516f2a0396ded4f14d119c7cb0ae9d4cba8e821386a",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is potty training resistance?",
        "text_sha256": "f5d94bb1f2580497ad386bc106de59e919c1fef00bc95deb033d4a9449c3d774",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Potty training resistance is just what it sounds like: when a child is capable of being potty trained but just doesn't want to.",
        "text_sha256": "3ae7292b68e252d562e85d7b625978725b6545b37aafa4483589aa5b91615a4e",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Instead of agreeing to try the toilet (which he always says no to when you ask), your tot continues to go to the bathroom in his diapers. He might also specifically ask to keep wearing diapers or even try to hold in his poop, which could cause him to become constipated .",
        "text_sha256": "b6f9ca7577dc6cb4d68abefff4318de69bc76f34733b99052b9209c87b4bf602",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“My girl is so set on not wanting to go on the potty,” says What to Expect Community member dawnm5. “She said she’s a baby and needs a diaper. I tried the naked method, and she will hold her pee all day until I put the diaper on for bed. Even if I get her to sit on it, she just won’t go.”",
        "text_sha256": "780cb085983ee3c5dbbf4a84459086bb3481547f1de8a79d0a29de9a696052a4",
        "word_count": 63
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Why your toddler refuses to potty train",
        "text_sha256": "04c91068c67c8c8c0d1fb3b227456591249a323f82e5e23da701b575f7a2ddbe",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "For a toddler, control is often the ultimate goal. He might not be able to dictate how long you stay at the playground or whether peas get served for dinner. But he can call the shots on where and when he decides to pee or poop.",
        "text_sha256": "0a7397f763c941ebf260714460db6a4a167c699981cae118060863d1213c5faf",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "So if he's overwhelmed by authority or just wants to test how far he can push the limits, he might meet your growing potty insistence with increasing potty resistance.",
        "text_sha256": "16726ff29eb372ff6a459b444c116eecd689dd6bae87e46a3e3aa252b63b5c41",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Fear can play a role too. Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsEmotional Issues and Potty Training ProblemsSee All Sources [1] Some children are terrified of falling into the toilet or are scared of the flushing mechanism (\"Hey, if stuff disappears down that hole, I might too!\") or the loud noise flushing makes. Some toddlers may also worry that they're actually losing a part of themselves when they poop and flush.",
        "text_sha256": "60977736bc63c9f089971f3b63295d28c4005c1df05a57adfa095a19e9f8a027",
        "word_count": 69
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsEmotional Issues and Potty Training ProblemsSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "672761e627ba23f891fb8858f514c924e60d416b6326e9802f6ca8562703fc83",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Signs of potty training resistance",
        "text_sha256": "2db7b46d74f04c40b8c615d819743eb4b65265c999a7865bcdf312588c6fa11a",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There's little mistaking being in the throes of potty training resistance. If trying to get your toddler to use the toilet feels like a constant battle — even though you know or believe he's capable of potty training — it's happening. Your tot might exhibit the following signs of potty training resistance:",
        "text_sha256": "a6859c1c9f6ce1d88c6ae4bd1af81f49c84bae23d42936bab301defe01f3e9a1",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Refusing to sit on the potty.",
        "text_sha256": "0db18fe764d4969d8f57c86ad5c9e8701ba83b69144a262ff19ee0768c77b426",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Being scared of sitting on the potty.",
        "text_sha256": "aa9afc9318df5b50ddac178552fcf2a1232a83a8cf70ffbf88ba160c9049c24c",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Peeing or pooping in his diaper on purpose.",
        "text_sha256": "9e7da840e6e1e72d202d9d2d65b3de2a6c3cf8e82e34d03cb5cf21858058cb1f",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Holding back pee or poop.",
        "text_sha256": "ebf4bf7117372ec2a8cf6bcc4c915b7a1e52b9ffb2a5addb8b2536344148afff",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Experiencing pain or burning when peeing or constipation (from holding it for too long).",
        "text_sha256": "70c482917041c112a80e3a780ed26bdc59f704811d3b883863da378e993978ae",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Ways to overcome potty training resistance",
        "text_sha256": "570286f1200e4987bff566f41e00fdc50e5f8483c9f8f08b3db2161cc55d8bfa",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There are several steps you can take to try to help your child get into potty training and get out of this stubborn \"I don't want to!\" phase:",
        "text_sha256": "f904413f0a1b266d3970a32e3ada2e41e178d4653448ecf687df2d6362b05a3d",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Make it your child's choice. Let him know he can switch to big boy underwear or disposable training pants and use the potty whenever he wants to, and that you're there to help when he asks. Then give it a rest and don't talk about it for a while. Remember: The more you push him, the more likely he is to push back.",
        "text_sha256": "5f88d19d1a067b5c656be7306528ac6d76371e58f1bcb8a7247181374b2b2287",
        "word_count": 63
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Keep calm. Losing your cool probably won't change your child's mind, and it might scare him.",
        "text_sha256": "86d59107ba49ba3ac85375d352035abab65b13cb2c7d17742301d0d795ca2adf",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Ease his fears. If your tot is afraid of the toilet's flushing sound or falling in, support his arms while he balances on the seat (or use a potty seat ). You can also refrain from flushing until he's out of the room, then gradually get him used to the sound.",
        "text_sha256": "e7acf8fd716d19b379ebccf67790e1264649e7633f647dc7a85c7d15d4c8eff8",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Offer control in other areas. If you give your child choices in what to wear or what to eat for lunch , he may be less likely to resist when it comes to the toilet.",
        "text_sha256": "17c7ce35e16200099fb8a6814e54342334cf797387916ea8f497c433a5b36197",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Provide an incentive. Without making a big deal of it, casually offer a prize like placing stickers on a chart for every potty success and giving a reward after a certain number is collected. (But phase out these rewards once he's warmed up to pottying.)",
        "text_sha256": "54ae35136f52a99a6b0a0b78974f56dd830b5c5824e8c6b7745dd62f35411ad5",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Read books about the potty. Stories of big kids or heroes using the toilet can be especially helpful if your toddler's main barrier is fear.",
        "text_sha256": "f0e6d40e60da64e4b3a1995798f864817f7e7bf44becb954d7019c2cb43a0256",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Recruit help. Ask a neutral adult figure, such as your child's babysitter or a grandparent, to put in a plug for the potty. Often a comment from an outside figure will have more of an effect than the pleadings of a parent. You can point out how an older sibling, cousin, or friend uses the potty too.",
        "text_sha256": "3713e84928a883b9fbd534f40f4ff9336d775334f547405f4a96508a13ca238d",
        "word_count": 57
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Don't call him a baby. Criticizing him for wanting to wear diapers and saying that it's babyish will likely backfire. Same goes for punishing him for not trying the potty or having an accident.",
        "text_sha256": "92d4c60abe0498135f4f0dacf7d9385bc9fe28d5d118be42071f76f88ce834a5",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Take a break and be patient. Make it a non-issue and eventually your child will relinquish his diapers. (Yes, it will happen.)",
        "text_sha256": "11dab9d09ef656ae102e70affa6bc5ca3d7262ab77a8963d2405cb1ecd102b39",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Want more potty training tips? Find them in the What to Expect app , where you can get expert advice and connect with other parents going through it too.",
        "text_sha256": "0c48e87c694e37f18e2e1e43ee8f14a9710dd9bcd9c40f9a421e4aa77b8a79e8",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When to call the doctor",
        "text_sha256": "ff3435591909fdafdceb4713bef36806db5b40f76c40294b17508b3f210e476c",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It's common for your toddler to push back about using the potty from time to time. (Remember, control!) But in some cases, prolonged potty training resistance could be a sign of a behavioral or health problem. Let the pediatrician know if:",
        "text_sha256": "dcf9c9419806443b0b5185196f19c6c76cb09d5e9a36b5ed5bcae5ccf418656f",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Your child is 3 1/2 and still hasn't gotten on board with potty training.",
        "text_sha256": "45e4396116c0b470d756a864bc33b7e1e35686783429a5a75373e3b597dc4bdf",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Your child has been resistant for several weeks, even though you feel like you've tried everything.",
        "text_sha256": "675c6f44c644b1a635bb80254369c9029260039c272dd19954719c85685c19b4",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Your child says it hurts or burns when he pees.",
        "text_sha256": "b70569a5b22243b0ac307852b830f4e2e740ba0d2cce3a3a53a35e373f8720a5",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "You suspect that your child is holding back his poop or that resistance is making him constipated.",
        "text_sha256": "32ffce1fa83615396ac5a574a98b005a6c3bcb19bbe9ccf72a2cde82a4ccf992",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "You notice blood in your child's urine or stool.",
        "text_sha256": "4c326ba98cd674674e889d506ca7983085df6b376d691b7d63af648832655b75",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Like walking or talking, potty training is a developmental skill that children master at their own speed. That's worth repeating — they'll do it when they're ready, not when you are. Some are up for it before 24 months, others not until after age 3. Most kids fall somewhere in between.",
        "text_sha256": "edf083f4614bdd00389f5533825f05ea2ee7b5857c79d9cb8648679df89a852a",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Whenever your child is ready to take the plunge, keep in mind that the age at which he finally gives up his diapers has nothing to do with intelligence or success in other skills. So be patient. He'll be using the potty like a pro before too long.",
        "text_sha256": "864564a39834cf1d622db3a7c5b943a0fe303eb5e0babfeb21e29e7d93f9d7b1",
        "word_count": 48
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 1302,
    "heading_count": 7
  },
  "title": "Potty Training Resistance: Why Your Toddler Won’t Use the Potty and How You Can Help",
